# Darksidebar-11 Cursor Rules
# Always strictly adhere to PROJECT_RULES.md:
# 1. Bump version with Semantic Versioning (SemVer) upon any fix or feature.
# 2. Build the rmskin package using ./build-package.ps1 -Version <NEW_VERSION>.
# 3. Update the Scoop manifest in bucket/darksidebar-11.json (version, url, sha256 hash from GitHub release).
# 4. Commit, tag (v<VERSION>), push to GitHub, and verify GitHub Actions release.
# 5. Strict Depersonalization: Repository and release .rmskin packages MUST NOT contain developer personal data (personal disks C/D/E/G/T/W, SyncMaster/DISPLAY2 monitor, Tyumen city). Repo files must contain clean templates (Primary monitor, 1 disk C:, London default, FirstRunDone=0).
# 6. Personal developer settings live ONLY in local Documents\Rainmeter\Skins\Darksidebar-11\ and must never be committed to GitHub.
# 7. Encoding rule: All .ini and .inc skin files MUST be encoded in Windows-1251 (CP1251). Never use UTF-8.
# 8. User Settings & Disk Preservation: Updates (via Scoop or .rmskin) must NEVER overwrite user Settings.inc or disks. All settings mirror to persistent external storage %APPDATA%\Rainmeter\Darksidebar11-Config. Scoop uninstaller must NEVER delete user skin folder. first-run.ps1 restores from persistent backup if available.


